37
00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:15.980
Almost forgot about that part. The benefits cascade beyond medicine in ways that should be obvious but apparently aren't.

38
00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:21.480
Addiction is a neurological disorder; cure the brain chemistry and the drug trade collapses.

39
00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:27.000
Most poverty is catastrophic medical costs; cure the diseases and people can work again.

40
00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:35.220
Radicalization is often untreated mental illness; you can't bomb someone into being mentally stable (you tried this, it

41
00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.700
didn't work, cost eight trillion dollars, created more radicals).

42
00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.900
Fix the biology and you fix the society. This is not a new insight.

43
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:49.600
It's just one your species keeps forgetting because explosions are louder than pharmacology.

44
00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:58.500
The Formulas. The Captured Dividend (the money you definitely get): The Societal Dividend (the money you save by being slightly

45
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:07.180
less insane): The indirect cost of war is calculated by combining environmental damage, loss of military growth, loss of

46
00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:12.300
capital due to conflict, and psychological costs. The Elasticity Question.

47
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:21.660
The elasticity parameter, e equals one point zero, asks the only interesting question here: if you cut military spending

48
00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:30.120
one percent, do war costs actually drop one percent too? Or do humans, being humans, find a way to keep killing each other

49
00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:36.700
