50
00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:41.680
Only a quarter of cuts reduce violence. e equals zero point five.

51
00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:46.360
The "humans are somewhat rational" scenario. Historically optimistic.

52
00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.100
e equals one point zero. Full match. The baseline assumption.

53
00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:56.720
Probably generous given your track record. e is greater than one point zero.

54
00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:02.360
The "curing cancer together is better bonding than threatening each other with missiles" scenario.

55
00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:06.320
Suspiciously wholesome. Here's the thing: it doesn't matter.

56
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:14.220
Even with the most pessimistic assumption (e equals zero point two five), the Captured Dividend of twenty-seven point two

57
00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:20.220
billion dollars is guaranteed. That money moves regardless of whether you manage to be less violent.

58
00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.600
It's a bank transfer, not a prayer. The Part Where the Math Gets Embarrassing.

59
00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:31.790
One. Guaranteed money: twenty-seven point two billion dollars annually.

60
00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.670
Direct budget transfer. If the treaty passes, this happens.

61
00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:42.400
No elasticity, no assumptions, no hoping humans behave. Just math.

62
00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:48.820
Two. Best case: Total societal benefit reaches one hundred and fourteen billion dollars annually.

63
00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:58.860
The range is wide because, again, your species. Three. Worst case: Even pessimistic scenarios stay above roughly fifty billion

64
00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:05.580
dollars annually. Your "worst case" is still the largest increase in medical research funding in human history.

65
00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:14.820
Four. Context: The Captured Dividend alone would boost global medical research funding by forty percent over the current

66
00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:22.320
sixty-seven point five billion dollar baseline. You've been spending more on camouflage paint than on curing Alzheimer's.

67
00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:28.240
What You're Assuming (and Where It Gets Shaky). The G.D.P. Multiplier.

68
00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:32.080
Spend a dollar on weapons, get sixty cents of economic value.

69
00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.670
Spend a dollar on healthcare, get four dollars and thirty cents back.

70
00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:45.440
Your species chose weapons. Every time. For centuries. I've watched you do this for four thousand, two hundred and ninety-seven

71
00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:54.660
years and it has never once gotten less baffling. The Lost Economic Growth component (two point seven two trillion dollars)

72
00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:00.060
already captures this difference. It's not double-counted, just consistently ignored.

73
00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:09.660
The Elasticity Assumption. The treaty requires multilateral cuts, so relative military balance is preserved; if your neighbor

74
00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:16.640
also cuts one percent, neither of you is weaker, you're just both slightly less armed, which historically has never been

75
00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:23.060
the problem. The Societal Dividend assumes one percent less spending means one percent less war cost.

76
00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:30.580
Reality is messier. Some costs lag by years. Some wars are fueled by boredom rather than budgets.

77
00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:37.960
And military spending may occasionally deter a war (though it starts far more than it prevents, which is a bit like crediting

78
00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:41.260
your arsonist neighbor for occasionally calling the fire department).

79
00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:48.760
How Good Are the Sources? I'm being honest about confidence levels, which is more than your defense contractors do.

80
